Z||000000||burdell1||11-14-2001||02:45 PM||||Does anyone know of someplace in the Twin Cities that will do an engine replacement on a Fiero relatively cheap? I have a Fiero that I need to move asap (I'm moving out of my apartment at the end of the month.)However, instead of towing the car 3 hours away to my parents house, I'd rather have it towed someplace nearby (in Minneapolis) and have it fixed. Any suggestions? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||11-14-2001||03:05 PM||||I had mine originally done at some guy's house... wouldn't recommend him again.  I've also had engine replaced at "Farmington Auto" ...don't recall just how expensive they were- I just wouldn't call them <I>cheap</I>.  <P>Maybe check with KEV (Kevin Lindeman-  <A HREF="mailto:black85gt@yahoo.com">black85gt@yahoo.com</A> )- he has offered his engine replacement services before... he may be interested (I think he's near Eden Prarie).<P>Hope this helps somehow...<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||troydeb||11-14-2001||05:44 PM||||Minn do you know if either of those 2 places could do a v8 swap?||||reg||1
Z||000003||MinnGreenGT||11-14-2001||05:54 PM||||Troydeb- welcome to the forum!<P>I certainly wouldn't expect "Farmington Auto" to do a V8 swap... and I don't believe that KEV has ever done one.  But if you gave Kevin enough time and all the right materials, I'm pretty confident that he'd be capable of doing it.  <P>Otherwise when it comes to doing V8 swaps... the best thing you could possibly do (aside from attempting it your self) is to go straight to the source: <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com" TARGET=_blank><B>Archie</B></A>.  He has done hundreds (if not close to a thousand?) V8 conversions.  He guarantees his work- and you know he can do it right the first time.  If you do it yourself using his kit, he's there for support whenever you need him.  I can't think of another Fiero vendor who comes more highly recommended by his customers.  Oh yeah, he's also close (just outside the Chicago area).<P>Here's his play-by-play on a ZZ4 TPI motor: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/014783.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/014783.html</A> <P>And Here's the play-by-play on a 350 Carbed Motor (going to a F355 spyder Conversion): <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/014468.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/014468.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||troydeb||11-15-2001||05:00 PM||||thanks for the info minn it helped alot in my search..||||reg||6
